.TH KLVTOOL-INSPECT 1 "1970-01-01" "klvtool dev" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
klvtool\-inspect \- Inspect an MPEG\-TS stream inventory, packet counts, and continuity diagnostics.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
klvtool inspect \-\-input <path\-or\-url> [\-\-view auto|pretty|raw] [\-\-duration <dur>] [\-\-idle\-timeout <dur>] [\-\-max\-packets <N>] [\-\-record <path>] [\-\-header "K: V"] [\-\-iface <name>]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Inspect an MPEG\-TS file or live stream and report its program / stream inventory, per\-PID packet counts, PES PTS bounds, and transport\-layer continuity diagnostics.
.PP
This is the entry point when triaging an unknown file: it surfaces likely metadata PIDs (KLV / data streams) so a follow\-up `klvtool decode \-\-pid <PID>` can target the right stream without scanning everything.
.PP
\-\-input also accepts URLs (udp://, tcp://, http(s)://, rtsp://, srt://, or '\-' for stdin). For live sources, inspect snapshots the PMT and per\-PID counts over the run window — bound the window with \-\-duration or stop with Ctrl\-C.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-duration\fR \fI(default 0s)\fR
stop after this wall\-clock duration (e.g. 30s, 5m, 1h); 0 disables
.TP
\fB\-\-header\fR
extra HTTP request header in 'Key: Value' form (repeatable; e.g. \-header "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"). HTTPS only — RTSP servers must embed credentials in the URL until token\-auth is wired up.
.TP
\fB\-\-idle\-timeout\fR \fI(default 0s)\fR
stop if no inbound bytes are observed for this duration; 0 disables
.TP
\fB\-\-iface\fR
egress network interface for UDP multicast joins (Linux: device name like eth0, or a local IP)
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR
MPEG\-TS input path or URL (file://, udp://, tcp://, http(s)://, rtsp://, srt://, or '\-' for stdin)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-packets\fR
stop after this many TS packets are observed; 0 disables
.TP
\fB\-\-record\fR
tee inbound source bytes to this file (works for any \-\-input, including a regular file)
.TP
\fB\-\-record\-overwrite\fR
allow \-\-record to overwrite an existing file (default refuses; honors O_CREATE|O_EXCL semantics)
.TP
\fB\-\-view\fR \fI(default auto)\fR
presentation mode: auto, pretty, or raw
.SH "EXAMPLES"
List streams and find likely KLV metadata PIDs
.RS 4
.nf
$ klvtool inspect --input mission.ts
.fi
.RE
.PP
Snapshot a live UDP multicast feed for 10 seconds
.RS 4
.nf
$ klvtool inspect --input "udp://239.0.0.1:5000?iface=eth0" --duration 10s
.fi
.RE
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
success
.TP
\fB1\fR
transport read failure (file unreadable, malformed, or truncated beyond recovery)
.TP
\fB2\fR
invalid usage
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
disable ANSI color in pretty output
.SH "REQUIRED TOOLS"
ffmpeg, ffprobe
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBklvtool\fR(1),
\fBklvtool\-decode\fR(1),
\fBklvtool\-diagnose\fR(1)
.SH "EXTERNAL REFERENCES"
.TP
\fBITU\-T H.222.0 / ISO/IEC 13818\-1 — MPEG\-TS systems layer\fR
https://www.itu.int/rec/T-REC-H.222.0
